GPTgrep includes a modified copy of the LiteParse PDFium Rust wrapper.
Upstream: https://github.com/run-llama/liteparse
Revision: ab8879623ee45a0b7a775d12b42a9a7ae9dab16b
Package: liteparse-pdfium 1.11.0, Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
GPTgrep modifications expose an allocation-free annotation count and adapt the
manifest to a standalone pinned dependency. Original source hashes and changes
are recorded in UPSTREAM.json. Upstream reference checkouts are not modified.
GPTgrep also adds length-admitted Info and page-label getters and a count/depth-
bounded outline reader with cycle and destination validation. Legacy getters
are retained; the admitted readers do not initialize forms or run actions.
GPTgrep additionally exposes checked page-object counts, raw object kinds and
fill rules, and allocation-free segment discriminants. These accessors retain
getter failures; geometry interpretation remains in the GPTgrep parser.
